# Technical Interview Guide: Code Debug AI Agent & Team

This document outlines the architecture, execution pipeline, tech stack rationale, security design, weak points, and scaling bottlenecks of the stateful multi-agent AI software engineering team.

---

## 1. Project Summary & Core Problem

*   **What the Project Does**: The project is a stateful multi-agent AI system designed to automatically analyze, debug, modify, and review codebase repositories. It orchestrates specialized subagents to locate buggy code using semantic search (RAG), apply bug fixes over standard Model Context Protocol (MCP) file tools, execute test suites securely, and review diffs for regressions.
*   **Core Problem**: Manual iteration loops (code-edit-test-fail-retry) cost significant developer time. Standard LLM wrappers fail at scale because they lack state memory, struggle with repository context limits, cannot execute system files/test suites, and cannot safely review their own work in isolated sandboxes.
*   **Solution**: A cyclical state machine built on LangGraph that delegates specialized roles (Researcher, Coder, Tester, Reviewer) and feeds execution outcomes (test failures, code diffs, review feedback) back into a Supervisor agent for correction loops.

